            <ArticleTitle>Remembrances from an early follower and leader of the Association for Academic Surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-4804(17)30400-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jss.2017.06.009</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This reflection retraces the evolution of early followers and leaders. Social change and early contributions set the stage for the current Association for Academic Surgery. Perhaps the most important contribution was Dr. George Zuidema's theme of inclusiveness. AAS was a decade ahead of its time in that regard.</AbstractText>
